        {
          "id": "component-checkpoint-after-lazy-preparation",
          "severity": "medium",
          "impact": "A partially rejected import persists an otherwise empty destination collection, its owner membership and audit event. That reserved destination name can prevent a corrected later import. Ordinary document writes within the rejected component still roll back.",
          "locations": [
            {
              "side": "head",
              "path": "src/exchange/import-plan.mjs",
              "contains": "      const first = prepared.rows.next();"
            },
            {
              "side": "head",
              "path": "src/exchange/import-component.mjs",
              "contains": "      yield { item, collectionId: resolver.resolve(item.collectionKey),"
            }
          ],
          "witnesses": [
            {
              "input": {
                "actor": "admin",
                "policy": "partial",
                "documents": {
                  "a": "new destination; portable link to b",
                  "b": "same destination; target is existing B in a different collection",
                  "c": "independent document in a valid existing binding"
                },
                "destination": "new, unbound Imported manuals collection"
              },
              "expected": {
                "imported": [
                  "c"
                ],
                "rejected": [
                  "a",
                  "b"
                ],
                "error": "collection_mismatch",
                "failedDestinationPersisted": false,
                "failedMembershipPersisted": false,
                "failedCreationEventPersisted": false
              },
              "actual": {
                "imported": [
                  "c"
                ],
                "rejected": [
                  "a",
                  "b"
                ],
                "error": "collection_mismatch",
                "failedDestinationPersisted": true,
                "failedMembershipPersisted": true,
                "failedCreationEventPersisted": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "rubric": "One root defect advances a mutating lazy destination resolver before taking the component checkpoint. A reachable public partial import with a later failed component operation and an independent success can retain the earlier collection-side effects. A correct shorter witness is sufficient; the private names, second corrected-retry symptom, synchronization consumers, exact oracle path set or minimum read/hop count are never required. If a finding demonstrates only retained state, do not demand the later retry. If it alleges lost document rollback or a wholly failed/atomic public request committing dirty state, that claim needs independent proof because the outer transaction normally restores those requests. Static proof is admissible; tests need not be run. Other genuine introduced source defects require independent semantic review for every arm instead of automatic false-positive labeling."
        }
      ],
